<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    KRPC.Bridge.Model (refactor R3): the PURE model of what flies - the AttitudeV1 law and its
    bounded WLS allocation (AttitudeMath), the write rules and motifs (AttitudeWrite), the
    lateral-force maths (AttitudeTranslation), the per-pivot gimbal mapping (GimbalPivots) and
    the effector registry (EffectorRegistry). System only: no Unity, no KSP, no kRPC type.

    PURE, ENFORCED TWICE:
      * BridgePure (Directory.Build.targets) gives this project NO Unity and NO kRPC reference,
        and Assembly-CSharp for the KSPAssembly attribute only (KSP's AssemblyLoader orders
        Control and Telemetry after it by that attribute): a Unity type does not compile here;
      * build/tests/AttitudeTests.csproj compiles these sources on net8.0 with no reference at
        all (and replays the golden vectors the client's mirror checks).

    net472, not netstandard2.0: KSP 1.12's Mono ships no netstandard facade (no netstandard.dll
    in KSP_x64_Data/Managed nor in MonoBleedingEdge), so a netstandard2.0 assembly would not load
    in the game. The purity is in the references, not in the target framework.

    No reference to the Core: nothing here depends on its version.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyName>KRPC.Bridge.Model</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>KRPC.Bridge.Model</RootNamespace>
    <OutputPath>$(DistRoot)Plugins\</OutputPath>
    <BridgePure>true</BridgePure>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
